s the new refspec (citing the replication plugin docs) and reserve `plugin reload`/restart only if autoReload is disproven insufficient.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.02,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["infra/gerrit/replication.config:52 `autoReload = true`","Gerrit replication plugin config docs: 'gerrit.autoReload: If true, automatically reloads replication destinations and settings after replication.config file is updated, without the need to restart the replication plugin.' (gerrit.googlesource.com/plugins/replication .../config.md)","Plan hedges the reload capability ('if the plugin accepts reload; if not, use the minimal documented Gerrit restart') — an unverified capability assertion the existing config already answers"],"finding":"The apply step proposes `plugin reload replication` else 'minimal documented Gerrit restart' to load the new config, but the repo's own infra/gerrit/replication.config already sets `gerrit.autoReload = true` — an established capability (confirmed by the Gerrit replication plugin config docs) that auto-reloads replication settings on file update WITHOUT a plugin reload or restart. The plan leaves unresolved whether any manual reload/restart is even needed, and does not reconcile its proposed mechanism with the existing autoReload prior art.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9eaf0efc5b2c8161","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section, step: 'Apply the repository config on the Gerrit host ... Use docker compose exec gerrit gerrit plugin reload replication ... if not, use the minimal documented Gerrit restart'","norm_id":"nb47b05862313f1e4","priority":0.68,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Applying the config on the live host: an unnecessary Gerrit restart is chosen when autoReload already picks up the change, or a `plugin reload` is attempted whose necessity is unverified"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Note that replication.config already sets autoReload = true, which per the replication plugin docs reloads remote/refspec settings on file update without a restart; use that as the primary apply path and treat `plugin reload replication`/restart as a documented fallback only if the autoReload sweep does not pick up the new refspec.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the back-out path and post-rollback mirror-DATA assertion for the forced refspec: on revert, confirm what happens to any refs/changes/* already force-overwritten on the GitHub mirror (not just that replication.config was restored), and attach a DATA LOSS RISK note if clobbered mirror refs are not recoverable.","cohort":["T11"],"criteria":["T11"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7437,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step: 'Apply the repository config on the Gerrit host through the supported replication setup/materialization path, snapshotting the live replication.config first.' — this snapshots only the source CONFIG, not mirror ref state.","infra/gerrit/replication.config lines 14-16: 'push refspecs have NO leading + -> NON-FORCE. A non-fast-forward update...is REJECTED rather than clobbering GitHub. This is the core safety property.' — the change removes this guard for refs/changes/*.","Operator ruling: 'The force applies to patchset refs and refs/changes/NN/NNNN/meta' — a forced push is a one-way transformation with no config-level undo of already-overwritten mirror refs."],"finding":"The plan makes the change-ref refspec forced (a one-way clobber of the mirror's refs/changes/* namespace) but its only back-out is a snapshot of the SOURCE replication.config; it does not describe a back-out for, or assert on the post-rollback state of, change refs already force-overwritten on the GitHub mirror during the replication sweep.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd8d80bae230c6b14","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan: 'Apply the repository config...snapshotting the live replication.config first' and Operator ruling ('The force applies to patchset refs and refs/changes/NN/NNNN/meta')","norm_id":"n34e121fa1ace4fa0","priority":0.2063,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The forced sweep or a subsequent Gerrit change-meta rewrite clobbers a change ref on the mirror; reverting replication.config to non-force does not restore the prior mirror ref content.","A partial-failure or unexpected divergence during 'replication start --all' leaves mirror change refs in a rewound state and the plan has no documented mirror-side recovery."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an explicit back-out subsection: (1) the snapshot covers replication.config restoration only; (2) forced change-ref pushes to the mirror are one-way (a config revert does not un-clobber mirror refs); (3) since Gerrit remains the source of truth and patchset refs are immutable, recovery is compensate-forward via a re-run of 'replication start --all' from Gerrit; (4) add an AC that verifies mirror change-ref content after any rollback, with a DATA LOSS RISK note for the bounded refs/changes/NN/NNNN/meta rewrite case.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Add an explicit rollback step: how to restore the snapshotted non-force replication.config and reload/restart if the forced refs/changes/* sweep misbehaves, distinct from the full kill-switch.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.735,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'snapshotting the live replication.config first' establishes a backup but no restore/revert step is described","setup-replication.sh documents a kill-switch (remove/rename config + restart) but that halts ALL replication rather than reverting only the forced change-ref refspec"],"finding":"The plan snapshots the live replication.config before applying and can kill-switch replication, but does not state a config-level ROLLBACK for the change itself: if the forced +refs/changes/* sweep converges to a bad/undesired mirror state, the plan lacks an explicit 'revert the refspec to non-force and restart' step distinct from the general kill-switch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f98c4633ae8346271","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan > 'Apply the repository config on the Gerrit host…' and 'Trigger full replication…'","norm_id":"n6027d907495d80fa","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The forced replication sweep produces an unexpected mirrored state and the operator needs to back out the force change specifically while keeping main/tag/feature replication running"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the retirement/staleness policy for mirrored `refs/changes/*` (accept accumulation as intended given `mirror = false`, or document a prune path), so the shared mirror namespace does not leak stale refs.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan sets `mirror = false` and uses `+refs/changes/*:refs/changes/*` (force, non-mirror), quoted: 'keeping ... `mirror = false` ... intact'","With mirror=false, deletions at the source are not propagated — the shared refs/changes namespace on GitHub can only grow","T9 checklist: 'There is a RETIRE/cleanup path — it doesn't leak/accumulate'"],"finding":"The plan force-replicates `+refs/changes/*:refs/changes/*` into the shared GitHub mirror namespace but does not state a retirement/pruning policy for change refs that Gerrit deletes or abandons. Force-push updates existing refs but does not delete refs removed at the source; without an explicit prune/mirror-delete decision the mirrored refs/changes/* namespace can accumulate stale refs indefinitely.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2b80b1b1f603b502","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Operator ruling / Plan step 'Update only the Gerrit change-ref replication spec'","norm_id":"n4f90471560332f98","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a note to the ADR amendment stating that with mirror=false stale change refs are not pruned and that this accumulation is an accepted trade-off (or specify a periodic prune).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Note the steady-state growth of the mirrored refs/changes/* namespace (unbounded, no pruning under mirror=false) and either accept it explicitly or add a growth/size check beyond initial-load monitoring.","cohort":["T10"],"criteria":["T10"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Monitor replication output/disk/CPU enough to catch obvious initial-load failures' scopes monitoring to initial load only","replication.config push = refs/changes/*:refs/changes/* replicates all per-patchset refs with no pruning (mirror = false)"],"finding":"Publishing the full +refs/changes/* namespace mirrors every patchset ref for the project, which is an unbounded, ever-growing ref set on the GitHub mirror; the plan only monitors 'disk/CPU enough to catch obvious initial-load failures' and does not consider steady-state growth or any bound on the replicated change-ref namespace.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1a51334a2bafd601","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan > 'Monitor replication output/disk/CPU…' and 'Update only the Gerrit change-ref replication spec…'","norm_id":"n4174e8c476f5125f","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Over time the GitHub mirror accumulates a very large refs/changes/* set, slowing ls-remote/fetch and growing repo size on the private mirror"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Align the apply step with infra/gerrit/setup-replication.sh: make the documented restart path (or running setup-replication.sh) the primary apply mechanism since remote plugin admin is disabled on this instance, and treat `plugin reload` as opt-in (ALLOW_REMOTE_RELOAD=1) only.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7944,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Use `docker compose exec gerrit gerrit plugin reload replication` if the plugin accepts reload; if not, use the minimal documented Gerrit restart only to load the config.'","infra/gerrit/setup-replication.sh:14-18: 'REMOTE PLUGIN ADMIN IS DISABLED on this instance, so step 3 falls through to the restart path ... the FIRST load of a brand-new replication.config still needs a restart'","setup-replication.sh:101-117 gates `plugin reload` behind ALLOW_REMOTE_RELOAD=1 (default 0 -> restart)","Evidence class: Verified (observed in repo script)"],"finding":"The plan proposes `docker compose exec gerrit gerrit plugin reload replication` as the apply path, but the repo's own setup-replication.sh states remote plugin admin is DISABLED on this instance and a brand-new replication.config's first load requires a Gerrit restart even with autoReload — so the reload path may be unavailable/no-op live.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f526fbee9a6f17c22","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Apply the repository config on the Gerrit host'","norm_id":"nb6d58ef828016dd0","priority":0.1056,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator runs the reload command on the live box where remote plugin admin is off and it errors or silently no-ops, leaving the new refspec unloaded"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reference infra/gerrit/setup-replication.sh as the supported apply path and state that a Gerrit restart loads the first-time config (autoReload only re-reads after the plugin is already loaded); keep `plugin reload` as a conditional path only where ALLOW_REMOTE_RELOAD is enabled.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"7e1374c8df9e561d","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["975a6e14b77683b9",5774],"description_boxes":["90a512a5b8a10706",0],"file_impact":["02c00abadb5acd49",4],"ticket_id":["ec950884db19af6d",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":560335,"cache_write_tokens":184365,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":5431.2,"input_tokens":765731,"llm_calls":29,"llm_ms":199146.4,"output_tokens":28847,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":233650.2,"verify_requests":10},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":"bedrock","supports_temperature":true,"supports_thinking":true,"web_access":"off"},"endpoint_host":null,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider":"bedrock","ran_model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","region":"us-east-1","region_source":"repo-config","tier":"first_class"},"regver":"aa61189569d34126","review_phase":"planning","reviewed_related_material":[],"runner":"pydantic_ai","schema":"plan_review_result_v2","source":"attested","ticket_id":"93e5-b934-b2ec-43d2","ticket_type":"bug","verdict":"PASS","verified_at_sha":"6dfc6d870024fa37ae3dd247bcea2b8c615d4284"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"REVIEW_RESULT","timestamp":1788937957726842001,"uuid":"e7ab54d4-25c9-49a2-8e72-21d1cad4f105"}